{"id": "EUVD-2026-55815", "enisaUuid": "09134a84-578e-33fb-8f33-143f2fc85a84", "description": "A flaw was found in Feast and feast-operator. The default configuration for both the Feast SDK and the feast-operator is \"no_auth,\" meaning no security manager is installed. This default allows unauthenticated and unauthorized access to feature-server, registry-server, and offline-server endpoints. A remote attacker, by exploiting this missing authentication, could achieve remote code execution (RCE) by storing a malicious User-Defined Function (UDF) on the feature-server, trigger a denial of service (DoS) by forcing re-materialization of all tenant features, and gain unauthorized access to cross-tenant data.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T20:44:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T11:10:07", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53261", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53262", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53263", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:84734", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-18941", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2511116"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2xfw-wg76-86w9", "CVE-2026-18941"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.9, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "27697006-1ee4-3918-8cfc-27fa403dd9e8", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1791868194"}, {"id": "2db830de-6718-3663-bd38-c4cdd04695ab", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1791833225"}, {"id": "4edcd296-a487-389d-b8ec-faac6f0832e1", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.3", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1786110033"}, {"id": "a5c6d773-0100-3b09-ad57-f908cbe0082e", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": 